    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d964-a2">

                <pb facs="0758" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg682"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Subsecretary of the Foreign
                            Office to Mr. Parker
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Querétaro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Representative</hi>: Replying to note No. 212,
                    dated November 15 last, in which you stated advices had been received to the
                    effect that the Yaqui Indians continued to commit depredations in the State of
                    Sonora, I am pleased to inform you that the citizen military commander of said
                    entity has been urgently recommended to impart protection to properties in that
                    region, national as well as foreign.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Siller</hi></signed>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">In charge of office</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
